{
  "_comment": "How a manifest claim is checked against the code. Same shape as tech-signatures.json, with one field that changes everything: absenceIsEvidence. A technology like XML always leaves a trace, so not finding it is an answer. A claim like `auth` does not: sign-in can be hand-rolled from a hash function and a database table, leaving no library behind, and concluding 'no sign-in' from 'no auth library' would be the over-confident exclusion this project exists to avoid. Only ci-cd and iac set it true, because those are files in the repository and a file that is not there is not there. Everywhere else, finding something proves it is used and finding nothing proves nothing.",
  "signatures": [
    {
