      "condition": "authorization-server",
      "absenceIsEvidence": false,
      "note": "Running an authorization server means running somebody's implementation of one. These are the libraries and products that are one, as opposed to the client libraries under `oauth`, which only talk to one. Libraries that are both, Authlib above all, are deliberately not listed as packages: a Flask app doing \"Sign in with Google\" installs Authlib as a client, and counting that as running a server would undo the distinction this condition exists to draw. Their server-side class names are in `source` instead. C# has no packages listed because `sv` does not read a `.csproj`; Duende IdentityServer and OpenIddict are found by the line that registers them instead.",
